  ],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Suppose we have some numbers and we arrange them in different possible orders.",
      "start_ms": 0,
      "end_ms": 5420,
      "start_frame": 0,
      "end_frame": 163,
      "word_count": 13
    },
    {
      "text": "Each different order is called a permutation.",
      "start_ms": 6400,
      "end_ms": 9420,
      "start_frame": 192,
      "end_frame": 283,
      "word_count": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "Now imagine, all of those permutations are arranged in increasing lexicographical order.",
      "start_ms": 10320,
      "end_ms": 17440,
      "start_frame": 310,
      "end_frame": 523,
      "word_count": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "Our job is not to find any bigger arrangement.",
      "start_ms": 18480,
      "end_ms": 21360,
      "start_frame": 554,
      "end_frame": 641,
      "word_count": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "We need the very next one, the smallest permutation that is still greater than the current permutation.",
      "start_ms": 21920,
      "end_ms": 28220,
      "start_frame": 658,
      "end_frame": 847,
      "word_count": 17
    },
    {
      "text": "For this lesson, our master array is 2, 1, 5, 4, 4, 3, 0.",
      "start_ms": 28220,
      "end_ms": 38840,
      "start_frame": 847,
      "end_frame": 1165,
      "word_count": 14
    },
    {
      "text": "We need to transform this same array into its next permutation.",
      "start_ms": 39580,
      "end_ms": 43800,
      "start_frame": 1187,
      "end_frame": 1314,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "And we have to do it in place.",
      "start_ms": 44360,
      "end_ms": 46500,
      "start_frame": 1331,
      "end_frame": 1395,
      "word_count": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "If a greater permutation does not exist, then we have to return to the smallest possible arrangement.",
      "start_ms": 47100,
      "end_ms": 53960,
      "start_frame": 1413,
      "end_frame": 1619,
      "word_count": 17
    },
    {
      "text": "So the real question is, how can we move to the next arrangement without generating every permutation?",
      "start_ms": 54530,
      "end_ms": 62840,
      "start_frame": 1636,
      "end_frame": 1885,
      "word_count": 17
    },
    {
      "text": "Before we solve that directly, let's first see the obvious approach.",
      "start_ms": 63900,
      "end_ms": 69180,
      "start_frame": 1917,
      "end_frame": 2075,
      "word_count": 11
    }
  ],
